00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:05.250 align:start position:0%
this video introduces Saku lee an  interactive technique that uses  screenshots to search and automate  graphical user interfaces  Sakuni search allows users to search a  documentation database using screenshots  of interface elements like this dialog  box the user draws a rectangle around  the dialog box to capture its screenshot  and submit it to Sakuni sakuni currently  searches a database of more than 50,000  screenshots from over a hundred computer  books it then returns a list of pages  containing the screenshots of the same  dialog box the user can browse and  select a page to read the details about  the style Sakuni script allows users to  write simple scripts to automate GUI  interaction by screen shots consider  this bus tracking interface with sakuni  script a user can draw a rectangle  around the bus symbol to take its  screenshot and select a neighborhood on  the map to watch for the bus arrival  also by taking a screenshot  after taking the screenshots the user  can use them directly in a statement  asking Sookie we've defined the  neighborhood on the map look inside and  find the bus symbol if such a symbol is  found a pop-up window can be displayed  to notify the user the bus has arrived  Sakuni script supports many visual  commands it can be used to click on  visual targets to drag a visual target  onto another visual target  to type a string in a visual target in  this case the Google search box in the  web browser with Saku Lee what you see  is what you search and what you see is  what you script
 

